{
  "id": "khorasani_bakhshi",
  "name": "Bakhshi (Khorasani dotar bards)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bardic music of the bakhshis of Khorasan in northeastern Iran, who sing epic and romance narratives, mystical poetry and lyric songs in Kurmanji Kurdish, Khorasani Turkic, Turkmen and Persian while accompanying themselves on the dotar, a long-necked two-string lute. The Persian-speaking school of Torbat-e Jam and the northern schools around Quchan and Bojnurd form distinct regional styles, and the Music of the Bakhshis of Khorasan is inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List. The dutar card, in its Turkmen bagshy setting (Turkmen-language bakhshis are one of Khorasan's own schools), stands in for the Khorasani dotar.",
  "recipe": "classic modern bakhshi, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. turkmen long necked bagshy tradition turkmen bagshy song accompaniment dutar. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
